{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"advisory":[{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a direct assertion that repr(subprocess_env({...})) equals/contains 'SubprocessEnv(<N values redacted>)' with the correct count and leaks no values.","criteria":["tests"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["tests/_subprocess_env.py:19-20: def __repr__(self) -> str: return f\"{type(self).__name__}(<{len(self)} values redacted>)\"","ABSENCE: search for 'repr' and 'redacted' in tests/unit/test_subprocess_env_repr_security.py returns no matches — no direct assertion on repr output","tests/unit/test_subprocess_env_repr_security.py:265: assert _SENTINEL_VALUE not in result.stdout + result.stderr (asserts value absence only, not repr shape)"],"finding":"The positive form of SubprocessEnv.__repr__ — that it renders the documented redacted diagnostic 'SubprocessEnv(<N values redacted>)' with a count reflecting the mapping size — is never directly asserted. The oracle tests only assert the sentinel VALUE is absent from traceback output; no test pins the redacted repr's shape or that it still yields a useful (non-empty) diagnostic. A regression where __repr__ returns e.g. an empty string or drops the count would still keep the value absent and pass all tests, degrading diagnosability without detection.","id":"0","impact":0.3,"location":"tests/_subprocess_env.py:19","norm_id":"n5f35f2af891a4a69","priority":0.3,"reason":"default-advisory","reviewer_id":"code-review-tests","reviewers":["code-review-tests"],"scenarios":["A future edit changes __repr__ to return '' or an unhelpful string; values remain redacted so security tests pass, but pytest diagnostics silently lose the '<N values redacted>' marker."],"se